    "No query-specific permeability, efflux, intestinal metabolism, or hepatic clearance data are supplied; L6 records are for other molecules and include different assay systems and species.",
    "No experimental data address ester hydrolysis, first-pass metabolism, or dissolution for the query.",
    "The most structurally similar ester context (pethidine) was measured in cirrhosis, which can elevate F by reducing first-pass metabolism; normal-condition transfer is uncertain."
